# Three players: Adeline's "for each opponent" makes one Human per opponent (CR 508.4), each tapped and attacking that
# opponent. Black Lotus pays for Adeline on turn 1 so she can attack on Bot1's second turn (T4). Adeline attacks only
# Bot2 as declared; the Humans were put onto the battlefield attacking Bot2 and Bot3 respectively, so Bot3 takes 1 and
# Bot2 takes Adeline's power (3 creatures: herself and two Humans) plus 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Adeline, Resplendent Cathar
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Adeline, Resplendent Cathar > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Adeline, Resplendent Cathar > Bot2; Human Token > Bot2; Human Token > Bot3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Power = 3
[T4 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot3.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Human Token; Human Token
